    "/digital/collection": {
      "route": "/digital/collection",
      "title": "MEDIEVAL BESTIARY ENTRIES.ORG",
      "content": [
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "MEDIEVAL BESTIARY ENTRIES.ORG"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2023"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "HTML, P5js"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Medieval Bestiary Entries.org, a minimalist HTML website, channels the rudimentary aesthetic of early internet pages, showcasing '10 medieval bestiary entries' featuring depictions of animals and descriptive texts. However, a visit to the sources page reveals a revelation: the images are synthesized using stable diffusion techniques, reflecting the propagation of misinformation and the ambiguity of truths seen in medieval bestiaries. This comparison underscores the broader issue of fake news and misinformation in our modern digital landscape, urging critical examination and caution in navigating today's influx of information and imagery."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "SIPHONOPHORA"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2023"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "HTML, P5js"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Siphonophora offers an immersive web experience inspired by siphonophores, colonial organisms that collaborate to form a unified whole. Through responsive movement mirroring the creatures' instinctive nature, users interact with the digital representation, witnessing cells undergoing a cloning process after 60 seconds, mirroring the growth patterns observed in siphonophores. This simulation invites users to engage with the collaborative dynamics and growth processes of these fascinating organisms, providing a glimpse into their unique collective behavior."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "VANITAS"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2023"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "PIKA, Silicone, Wood"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "\"Vanitas\" is an installation that explores the consequences of excessive luxury, featuring classical paintings morphing into macabre depictions through AI. This cautionary piece urges contemplation on the dangers of unchecked desires, serving as a stark reminder to tread carefully in the pursuit of material pleasures."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "DECODING DISEASE"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2023"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "VR, Runway ML"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "\"Decoding Disease\" is a virtual reality art installation that immerses visitors in the unique perspective of an artificial intelligence's gallery. These materials are generated by ai and prompted by diseases, gaining insight into the AI's interpretation of the most human afflictions, both from a societal and scientific standpoint."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "I_THINK_THEREFORE_ I _AM_HUMAN"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2022"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Processing, This person does not exist"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "A series of image comparisons of things that appear more or less human then the other"
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "GAMES GLITCHES AND CREATIVITY"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2023"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Html, Css, twine"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "A collection of HTML-based work for my Games Glitches and Creativity class."
        }
      ],
