    "/digital/this-is-my-stop": {
      "route": "/digital/this-is-my-stop",
      "title": "THIS IS MY STOP",
      "content": [
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "THIS IS MY STOP"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2026"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Best of Design"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Interactive narrative game / custom hardware"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Hardware designer"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Created during the 2026 Creative Hackathon, This Is My Stop is a moody interactive game set inside an abandoned subway car. A gyroscope air mouse is reimagined as a handheld flashlight, letting players search the dark environment and uncover its story one object at a time. The project received the hackathon's Best of Design award."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "THE EXPERIENCE"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "The room becomes part of the game. The player points the physical light toward a projected subway scene, and that motion moves the beam through the virtual car. Details emerge only when illuminated, turning exploration into a slow, tactile act of discovery."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "MY ROLE"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "As hardware designer, I developed and prototyped the handheld controller, adapting gyroscopic input into the flashlight interaction and helping integrate the physical device with the team's game. The rapid build moved from loose electronics and foam-board studies to a working playtest controller over the course of the hackathon."
        },
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "COLLABORATION"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Designed and built with Maiia Lysytska (game design), Miranda Derossi (narrative design and sound), Jacob Carlos (3D art and sound), and Ava Rose Mendelson (2D art). Sophie Katsivelos led hardware design."
        }
      ],
      "images": [
        "/assets/this-is-my-stop/installation-flashlight.jpg",
        "/assets/this-is-my-stop/team-development.jpg",
        "/assets/this-is-my-stop/hardware-prototype.jpg",
