          "tag": "p",
          "text": "“The Industrial Woman” is a commentary on the unappreciated and exploitative labor provided by housewives and its place in capitalism. Under capitalism, the role of the housewife is often considered a natural and necessary extension of women's innate nurturing and domestic abilities. However, this perspective overlooks the economic and social factors that shape the housewife's role and the exploitation that often accompanies it."
