    "/physical/african-bullfrog": {
      "route": "/physical/african-bullfrog",
      "title": "AFRICAN BULLFROG",
      "content": [
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "text": "AFRICAN BULLFROG"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "2026"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Foam, fiber glass, resin, polly cam."
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "Inspired by the naturalistic animal models at the American Museum of Natural History, this bullfrog sculpture bridges traditional fabrication and digital processes. The piece was hand-sculpted and textured in clay, molded in silicone with a fiberglass jacket, and cast as a fiberglass, foam-filled final. It was then hand-painted using airbrush and brush techniques, finished with a semi-gloss to achieve a lifelike wet-skin effect. The completed sculpture was 3D scanned using Polycam and printed at one-tenth scale in 8K resin, demonstrating how digital tools can extend and refine traditional sculptural workflows."
        }
      ],
