  "study": {
    "images": [
      "/assets/005-b80ef2c9295e.jpg"
    ],
    "content": [
      {
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "DIGITAL SOCIOLOGY STUDY"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Buttons, Composite board, Quest 3, buttons, Ada fruit bitsy,"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Made with: Unity, Maya, Blender, Substance Painter, cursor."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "2025"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Digital Sociology Study is a networked VR installation that examines how digital environments influence social behavior through feedback systems. Two players enter one of four open-ended virtual worlds—designed to prompt activities like dancing, building, or painting—without explicit instruction. Their interactions unfold naturally, shaped not only by each other but also by up to five hidden observers. A session lasts approximately five minutes at minimum."
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Viewing the experience through an arcade-style interface, the observers control the environment in real-time—altering lighting, sound, tools, and even the players’ avatars, including gender presentation. They respond with buzzers and sound effects, indirectly guiding behavior through signals of approval or disapproval."
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The piece explores how anonymity, constrained communication, and digital embodiment reshape social interaction. It asks whether stripped of identity and structure, people connect more authentically—or unravel. Ultimately, the work becomes a live experiment in how we perform, adapt, and relate under unseen influence."
      }
    ]
  },
  "about": {
    "images": [
      "/assets/042-e51153cae8a9.png"
    ],
    "content": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Sophie Katsivelos, a young designer residing in New York City, boasts a diverse portfolio spanning from roles as an assistant costume designer to a consulting design intern. Her design interests span various disciplines, with a particular penchant for interactive and immersive design."
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Sophie explores how new technology can spur connection and meaningful memories. She is dedicated to crafting compelling narratives and impactful experiences. As of 2025, she has graduated from  PRATT Institute’s Art and Technology BFA program."
